{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Los Angeles RSO relocation assistance amounts","requirement":"When a tenancy is terminated for a reason requiring relocation assistance under the Rent Stabilization Ordinance, the landlord must pay the tenant the relocation amount for the unit within 15 days of service of the written notice of eviction.","key_value":"Eligible tenant $11,000 (under 3 years) or $14,400 (3+ years or low income); qualified tenant $23,150 or $27,400; per unit","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced from rental units covered by the Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance. Relocation assistance is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies when a tenancy is terminated for a no-fault reason requiring relocation; payment is per unit, not per tenant; the amount depends on the tenant's eligible or qualified status, household income and length of tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"A landlord may offset the tenant's accumulated rent against relocation assistance unless the relocation is owed because a governmental agency order to vacate or comply was issued for an unpermitted dwelling (LAMC 151.09.G,5., 165.06.J.).","penalty":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an action to recover possession and may file a complaint with LAHD.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §151.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"Eligible Tenant $11,000 $14,400 Qualified Tenant $23,150 $27,400","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Los Angeles JCO relocation assistance amounts","requirement":"When a tenancy is terminated for a reason requiring relocation assistance under the Just Cause Ordinance, the landlord must pay the tenant the relocation amount for the unit within 15 days of service of the written notice of eviction.","key_value":"Eligible tenant $11,000 (under 3 years) or $14,400 (3+ years or low income); qualified tenant $23,150 or $27,400; per unit","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced from rental units covered by the Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance. Relocation assistance is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies when a tenancy is terminated for a no-fault reason requiring relocation; payment is per unit, not per tenant; the amount depends on the tenant's eligible or qualified status, household income and length of tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Single-family dwelling subject to the JCO owned by a natural person owning no more than four dwelling units: one month's rent, and LAMC 151.30(E) does not apply. Accumulated rent offset applies except where a government order to vacate an unpermitted dwelling applies.","penalty":"A tenant may raise the landlord's failure to provide relocation assistance as an affirmative defense in an action to recover possession and may file a complaint with LAHD.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §165.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"When the residential real property is a single-family dwelling subject to the JCO and the owner is a natural person, including natural persons who hold properties in a trust or registered legal entity controlled by that natural person, who owns no more than four dwelling units and a single-family home on a separate lot in the City of Los Angeles: one month’s rent that was in effect when the landlord served the written notice to terminate the tenancy, as either a monetary payment or credit.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-02","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance payments for low-income tenants displaced by new construction","requirement":"Only lower-income households displaced by demolition of their units for new construction must receive relocation payments consistent with state redevelopment relocation benefits; those tenants receive at least the RSO or JCO amounts, increased only if state law requires.","key_value":"Extremely low income $115,480; very low income $96,750; low income $87,450","coverage_conditions":"Low, very low and extremely low income households displaced by new development (demolition of units for new construction) in the City of Los Angeles.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where the tenant is displaced by demolition for new construction and the household is low, very low or extremely low income; above low income tenants receive the RSO or JCO amounts instead.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Households above low income displaced by new development receive the RSO or JCO amounts in Chart A rather than the standardized RPO payments.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO)","quoted_span":"The City's Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) and the State's Housing Crisis Act (HCA) require that ONLY lower income households being displaced for the purpose of demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction must receive relocation payment consistent to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities pursuant to Chapter 16 (commencing with Section 7260) of Division 7 of Title 1 (Government Code 66300.6(b)(4)(A)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
